TITLE: fix: allow OAuth client tokens on GET /user, keep modifying actions blocked
## What

#2898 restricted OAuth client access tokens to OAuth endpoints. That also blocked `GET /user`, which breaks existing projects that read the user with these tokens (e.g. `supabase.auth.getUser()`).

This PR **temporarily** allows OAuth client access tokens on `GET /user` only. All modifying actions still reject them with `403 no_authorization`:

- `PUT /user`
- `/user/identities/*`, `/user/oauth/grants`
- `/factors/*`, `/passkeys/*`
- `/logout`, `/reauthenticate`
- `/admin/*`, `/invite`

## How

The `/user` group used to apply `requireAuthentication` to every route in it. Now each route sets its own middleware: `GET /user` uses `requireAuthenticationAllowOAuthClient`, and every other `/user` route keeps `requireAuthentication`. A comment on the route group says that new `/user` routes must add `requireAuthentication`.

## Note: this is temporary

`GET /user` returns `app_metadata`, the full `user_metadata`, identities and factors. That is more than the scopes an OAuth client is granted. We are reopening it for now so existing projects don't break. We will revisit this soon and reject OAuth client tokens on `/user` entirely. OAuth clients should move to `GET /oauth/userinfo`.

## Tests

`TestOAuthClientTokenRouteAccess` now covers:

- `GET /user` and `/oauth/userinfo` return 200 with an OAuth client token.
- The modifying endpoints above return 403 with an OAuth client token.
- A rejected `PUT /user` leaves the user unchanged.
