TITLE: Custom connector "Connector couldn't be added" right after authorization server metadata fetch (Supabase Auth)
**Connector URL:** https://suleytangun.com/mcp (self-hosted MCP server on Vercel, OAuth by Supabase Auth's OAuth 2.1 server)

**When:** every attempt on 13 Nov 2026, 15:51 to 16:08 GMT. It worked earlier the same day; the existing connection dropped around 11:24 GMT and can't be re-added since.

**What happens:** Add custom connector → "Connector couldn't be added. You can try again." No sign-in window opens.

**Server logs for each attempt (requests from 160.79.106.x):**
1. `POST /mcp` → 401 with `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm="mcp", resource_metadata="https://suleytangun.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource"`
2. `GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` → 200 (`resource: https://suleytangun.com/mcp`, `authorization_servers: [https://<project>.supabase.co/auth/v1]`)
3. `GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server` on Supabase → 200 (issuer matches, authorize/token endpoints, `code_challenge_methods_supported: ["S256","plain"]`, `client_secret_post` supported)
4. Nothing after that: no `/oauth/clients/register`, no `/oauth/authorize`.

**Tried:**
- Pre-registered confidential client (ID and secret in Advanced settings): same failure.
- Advanced settings left blank, with dynamic client registration switched on (metadata then includes `registration_endpoint`): same failure, and no registration request was made.
- New URL (`/mcp?v=2`), and signing out and back in: same failure.

**What works:** the same discovery and authorize flow with `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` 1.32.1 `auth()` against this server reaches the authorize redirect without errors. Opening the authorize URL by hand completes consent and redirects to `https://claude.ai/api/mcp/auth_callback`.

Claude support (Fin) suggested filing here so the team can trace what fails on Claude's side after step 3.
