TITLE: OAuth sign-in completes (DCR, Supabase Auth), then "it then refused Claude's request" and no authenticated request ever reaches the server
### MCP server URL

`https://belief-ids-shirts-given.trycloudflare.com/api/mcp/claude`

This is a cloudflared quick tunnel to a local instance of our server, used for this reproduction; it will not stay up. The same server will be at `https://app.studiolofi.com/api/mcp/claude` once this branch is deployed. The production host already serves the same server for the ChatGPT Apps SDK integration at `/api/mcp`, where sign-in and authenticated calls work.

### Where does the issue occur?

When auth finishes and redirects back to Claude.ai

### Transport used

streamable-http

### Client registration type

Dynamic Client Registration (DCR)

### SSE only: Does your server return the expected status code for POST requests?

Not applicable (my server does not use SSE)

### When did you last reproduce this?

2026-11-06, about 14:50 UTC (6:50 AM PST). First reproduced 2026-11-05 around 20:18 UTC on a previous tunnel hostname; same result.

### Browser and OS

Chrome on macOS

### Describe the issue

Custom connector added on claude.ai (web) with "Sign in now" and OAuth client "Register automatically". Dynamic registration succeeds, the user is sent to our consent page, signs in and approves, and is redirected back to Claude. Claude then shows "You signed in to Test Lofi, but it then refused Claude's request…" and the connector page says "Couldn't connect to the server. Check that the URL points to a valid MCP server."

From the server side, no request carrying an `Authorization` header ever arrives after the redirect. The only post-consent traffic is one more `GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/mcp/claude` (200). So the failure happens inside Claude between the token response and the first authenticated MCP request.

Our authorization server is Supabase Auth (issuer `https://hspijxomkfoapxydgpcj.supabase.co/auth/v1`). Reproducing Claude's flow by hand against the same issuer and server works end to end (details below), so we suspect a check Claude applies to the token that Supabase does not satisfy, most likely the audience: Claude sends the connector URL as `resource`, and Supabase issues tokens with a fixed `aud: "authenticated"` and no `resource` claim.

Same symptom as #1215 and #1018 (token exchange succeeds, connector never becomes active, no MCP call after the token).

### Issue details

```shell
Toast on claude.ai:
  "You signed in to Test Lofi, but it then refused Claude's request. Your account there
   may not allow access from Claude, or a firewall may be blocking Claude. Trying again
   may not help. Ask whoever manages your account there, or the support team for Test
   Lofi, to check your access. Claude support reference: ofid_012c4768473c1fa3"

Connector page:
  "Connection issue — Couldn't connect to the server. Check that the URL points to a
   valid MCP server." with a Reconnect button. Reconnect restarts authorization from the
   consent page and ends the same way.

Protected resource metadata served at
  GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/mcp/claude  -> 200
  {
    "resource": "https://belief-ids-shirts-given.trycloudflare.com/api/mcp/claude",
    "authorization_servers": ["https://hspijxomkfoapxydgpcj.supabase.co/auth/v1"],
    "scopes_supported": ["openid","email","profile"],
    "bearer_methods_supported": ["header"],
    "resource_policy_uri": "...", "resource_tos_uri": "..."
  }

Unauthenticated POST tools/call -> 401
  WWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata="https://belief-ids-shirts-given.trycloudflare.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/mcp/claude"
Unauthenticated POST initialize / tools/list -> 200 (lazy auth; the Add dialog
  therefore detects "No sign-in", we pick "Sign in now" manually)
GET /api/mcp/claude -> 405

Supabase Auth metadata (authorization server):
  registration_endpoint present
  code_challenge_methods_supported: ["S256","plain"]
  token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported includes "none"
  grant_types_supported: ["authorization_code","refresh_token"]
  scopes_supported includes "offline_access"
```

### Expected behavior

After the user approves on the consent page and is redirected back, Claude exchanges the code, calls `initialize` and `tools/list` with the bearer token, and the connector becomes active. That is what happens when we run the same steps by hand:

- Register a public client at Supabase's `registration_endpoint` (`token_endpoint_auth_method: "none"`, `grant_types: ["authorization_code","refresh_token"]`).
- Authorization request with S256 PKCE, `scope=openid email profile offline_access`, `resource=<connector URL>`; approve on the same consent page.
- Token request (form-urlencoded, `client_id`, `code_verifier`, `resource`) → 200 with `access_token` (JWT), `refresh_token`, `expires_in: 3600`, `token_type: bearer`. No `scope` field in the response.
- Access token claims: `iss` = the Supabase issuer, `aud: "authenticated"`, `client_id` = the registered client, `scope` = the requested scopes, no `resource` claim.
- With that token: `initialize` → 200, authenticated `tools/call` → 200. Refresh → 200 with a rotated refresh token.

### Logs from your server

```shell
# 2026-11-06, Next.js dev server behind the tunnel (request log has no per-line
# timestamps; the whole Connect attempt fell between 14:49 and 14:53 UTC).
GET  /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/mcp/claude  200   # Claude discovery
GET  /api/mcp/claude                                       405
POST /api/mcp/claude                                       200   # unauthenticated initialize
GET  /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server               404   # not served here; AS is Supabase
POST /api/mcp/claude                                       200   # tools/list, unauthenticated
POST /api/mcp/claude                                       200
POST /api/mcp/claude                                       200
# ... user signs in and approves on the consent page (served on our production host) ...
GET  /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/mcp/claude  200   # last request Claude sends
# no request with an Authorization header, ever

# 2026-11-05 (previous tunnel hostname), same sequence with timestamps:
20:10 UTC  GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/mcp/claude  200
20:18 UTC  Connect: DCR succeeded, consent page reached and approved,
           then one GET of the protected-resource document -> 200 and nothing else.
```

### Additional context

Questions we would like answered, since they decide how we ship this:

1. Does claude.ai require the access token's `aud` (or a `resource` claim) to equal the connector URL before it calls the server? If so, is there a supported path for authorization servers that do not implement RFC 8707, such as Supabase Auth?
2. Is a missing `scope` field in the token response treated as an error?
3. Would Anthropic-held client credentials (instead of DCR) change the outcome, given the token audience would be the same?

The Add dialog now also offers "Use Claude's published identity (CIMD)"; w
